      "text": "As a full-blooded and incredibly proud Tokelauan, born and raised in the beautiful country of New Zealand, my heart is overflowing with excitement as my family and I prepare to make our very first journey to Tokelau next year.\r\nAlthough I’ve never set foot on the islands before, Tokelau has always been a part of who I am. It lives in my blood, my heritage, and my identity. The thought of finally walking the land of my ancestors, meeting my people, embracing our traditions, and experiencing the beauty of our homeland is something I can hardly put into words. It feels like coming home to a place I’ve carried in my heart my whole life.\r\nThank you for creating such an incredible documentary. You didn’t just tell a story—you honoured our people with such warmth, dignity, and authenticity. The way you captured and articulated the beauty, resilience, and spirit of Tokelau was deeply moving. It has made me even more excited and grateful for the journey that lies ahead.\r\nFakafetai lahi. ❤",
